  "environment_assumptions": [
    "single event thread; cancellation observer and progress start/show callbacks may execute synchronously and reenter",
    "record/showQueued/recordProgress and transport are passive synchronous sinks in inherited schedules",
    "file is a stable object identity with immutable id/size and shared source; no entry file value mutation schedule is claimed",
    "decode returns either immediate frame or single-fulfillment deferred result; explicit resolution, no fixed sleeps",
    "decode rejection and physical transfer completion are not modeled by parent",
    "source events use snapshot listener dispatch semantics; listener removal does not retract accepted decode",
    "each accepted command queues synchronously; no concurrent-thread race introduced"
  ],
  "semantic_differences": [
    "Frontend components execute real framework lifecycle and project session state; all source events and reentrant sinks retain synchronous semantics.",
    "Native ports replace DOM signal ownership with native attempt objects and synchronous callable observers; bridge exposes a real physical AbortSignal to the injected transport only. Go cancellation uses context.CancelFunc; other ports use object-owned idempotent flags and language callbacks.",
    "Native decoding continuations are closures/blocks/function consumers invoked by the explicit source adapter on a later host turn; immediate decoding is never artificially deferred. No native Promise/framework lifecycle is claimed.",
    "Wire adapter interns stable file objects by token; native visit object identity and frame value payload remain distinct. No mutable-entry file snapshot relation is inferred.",
    "Internal cancellation observer registration precedes passive transport abort observers, matching the original signal registration order; both notifications stay synchronous and reentrant. Native public embedding ABI is candidate-visible; private helper names are not oracle assertions."
